      "side": 1,
      "message": "Dear Sir:\nTo your question1:\n    Please just submit your change to us and we will gladly take it as this is not an upstream driver codepath.\nAnswer1:\n    That is a feature designed by xiaomi/oppo/vivo. we add Vendor hook to handle other USB control transfer protocols designed by xiaomi/oppo/vivo. please help me review .\n\nTo your question2:\n    Also, what \"new cast protocol\" is needed to be supported here that we do not already support?\nAnswer2:\n    We need to add Vendor hook to handle other USB control transfer protocols usb_ctrlrequest-\u003ebRequest.The following code is our logic in vendor hook. it will \ncheck whether the ctrl-\u003ebRequest is UCAR_GET_VERSION and UCAR_GET_VERSION  is self data added by xiaomi.\nE.g:\nif (ctrl-\u003ebRequestType \u003d\u003d (USB_DIR_IN | USB_TYPE_VENDOR)) {\n\t\tif (ctrl-\u003ebRequest \u003d\u003d UCAR_GET_VERSION) {\n\t\t\t_ucar_setup_desc-\u003eversion \u003d UCAR_REPLY_VERSION;\n\t\t\tschedule_work(\u0026_ucar_setup_desc-\u003ework);\n\t\t\tvalue \u003d 0;\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tretValue \u003d min(w_length, (u16) 1);\n\treq-\u003elength \u003d retValue;\n\treq-\u003econtext \u003d cdev;\n\treq-\u003ezero \u003d retValue \u003c w_length;\n\t*(u8 *)req-\u003ebuf \u003d UCAR_REPLY_VERSION;\n\tretValue \u003d android_ep0_queue(cdev, req, GFP_ATOMIC);\n\tif (retValue \u003c 0) {\n\t\tDBG(cdev, \"ucar_ctrlreq: ep_queue --\u003e %d\\n\", retValue);\n\t\treq-\u003estatus \u003d 0;\n\t\tif (retValue !\u003d -ESHUTDOWN)\n\t\t\tandroid_setup_complete(cdev-\u003egadget-\u003eep0, req);\n\t}",
